          "text": "<|START_TEXT|>A process is an independent execution environment that contains its own memory space, system resources, and a thread of control. Each process runs a program and has its own virtual address space, file descriptors, and environment, so it can be scheduled by the operating system and run concurrently with other processes. Because processes are isolated, one crashing or misbehaving process typically does not affect others, but creating a new process incurs overhead in terms of memory and CPU usage.\n\nA thread, on the other hand, is a lightweight subunit of a process that shares the process\u2019s memory and resources with other threads in the same process. Threads exist within a single process"
