          "text": "<|START_TEXT|>A process is an independent program instance that has its own memory space, system resources, and execution context. When you launch an application, the operating system creates a process for it, complete with separate code, data, stack, and file descriptors. Processes are isolated from each other, so a crash or malicious activity in one process typically won\u2019t affect the others.\n\nA thread, on the other hand, is a lightweight subunit of a process that shares the process\u2019s memory and resources. Threads exist within a single process and execute concurrently, allowing the process to perform multiple tasks in parallel. Because they share the same address space, threads can communicate"
